('5314b5ec-c5cc-516d-a799-ef1b3df851c7'::uuid, 'ff9acfdf-8a70-5f66-a587-b852fbb9b715'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CLUP 2017-2027 (110 barangays) has a DRRM-CCA chapter but predates the CDRA. CDRA Final Report rates risk by likelihood and severity per hazard and cites GeoRiskPH damage estimates, but defines no explicit most-probable and most-severe scenarios.'),
('de671b65-6b61-57f3-b9b0-c88d94125ce2'::uuid, 'ff9acfdf-8a70-5f66-a587-b852fbb9b715'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) LCCAP 2019-2030 decision areas set high-risk barangays and values (29 barangays, 445.17 ha, PHP 13.36 B flood risk; 16 barangays, 297.6 ha of farmland) and name the Pagsangaan River as the key flood-control project; CDP 2024-2030 makes the CDRA database the basis for development planning (strategy 4). Neither defines most-probable and most-severe scenarios.'),
('ee0158e9-f6e7-5690-88cb-3905de426f3a'::uuid, '00ac2029-df8a-5b3b-bf2a-a329ea9c74cc'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CDRA 6.7.1 proposes ''share of development proposals screened against hazard information'' as a future indicator; CLUP 2.5.3 proposes an LDC monitoring team; DRRM sits in the LDC and LFC (A1.7). No screening form or LDC/LFC record sighted.'),
('c92b5ce1-9a05-5386-83d1-6f9553731867'::uuid, 'e8ab7e23-6b6f-54e5-9ce3-11546011ebea'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CDRA Final Report estimates exposure and risk for population (incl. informal settlers, light-material houses and households below poverty), urban use areas (PHP values), agriculture and fisheries production areas, critical-point facilities and lifelines; ecosystems are covered by qualitative impact chains.'),
('9f74e5b6-7dcb-569b-8db6-417c77447e44'::uuid, 'e8ab7e23-6b6f-54e5-9ce3-11546011ebea'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) LCCAP 2019-2030 names livelihood exposure (8,000 informal-economy workers, 1,686 fisherfolk, 4,540 farmers) and agricultural values at risk (PHP 13.16 M), and cites TY Yolanda agricultural damage (PHP 2.059 B) and the 2015-16 El Nino damage; jobs and income losses are still not quantified.'),
('ab3b954d-5489-5032-8713-09cb37ae0da4'::uuid, '3b3e1d71-ce84-5910-a09d-1fed44af6153'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'ZO (CLUP 2017-2027) requires a locational clearance before a building permit, Water Code easements, a 5-m Marina Fault easement and no-build zones; no flood, landslide or storm-surge overlay. CENRO/CDRRMO sit on the Local Zoning Review Committee.'),
('c3bb9db6-f51a-5316-9a09-30264f9b6160'::uuid, '1ccc93c6-a8b5-5701-9c55-497a0687abc6'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CDRA scores critical-point facility vulnerability (e.g., ECs and covered courts rated ''Poor''; most facilities lack landslide mitigation measures); 10-Yr Plan plans retrofitting of 30 ECs. No Building Official structural assessment or pre-impact inspection procedure sighted.'),
('1f1f944e-9947-5952-9114-191881559699'::uuid, '1ccc93c6-a8b5-5701-9c55-497a0687abc6'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDP 2024-2030 PPA 1.6 plans structural integrity assessment, infrastructure audit and an inventory of critical infrastructure (with regular positions); none done in the set.'),
('495bd618-513c-52a0-aa87-65b6c07b3753'::uuid, 'cd3c087e-ac5b-5aa6-bf83-eee0121a92a4'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'telco restoration MOA planned (10-Yr Plan); CDRA rates lifeline exposure by barangay and notes no lifeline utility is insured; CDRA MDA 2 recommends lifeline dependency maps and restoration priorities.'),
('d62f1ad7-9ef9-50b3-8ec2-045474a5ed17'::uuid, 'cd3c087e-ac5b-5aa6-bf83-eee0121a92a4'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) LEYECO V sits on the CDRRMC (EO 2024-032A); LEYECO V and NGCP Milagro are CDRA TWG partners (EO 2023-0025); CDP PPA 3.16 plans restoration of critical lifelines. No restoration-priority agreement sighted.'),
('8ea058a5-1aa5-5e24-94ae-ade09c56140e'::uuid, 'cd3c087e-ac5b-5aa6-bf83-eee0121a92a4'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(issuances 2021-2024, read 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 10 s.2021 (Odette) asked LEYECO V to use its 2 MW standby generator at Brgy. Alta Vista during widespread outages. Score 1 -> 2: one documented power arrangement used in an event; none for water or telecom, and no standing restoration-priority list.'),
('ba763cc5-f7c0-577f-9437-c764b667c59c'::uuid, 'ceaa2416-7b66-527c-a5c2-6b435b6ccc0b'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CDRA identifies high-consequence lifeline roads (e.g., Macabug Road, Sumangga Road, PNOC roads, Lake Danao Circumferential Road) and Ormoc Port''s exposure to storm surge; CDRA MDA 2 recommends identifying critical road segments, bridges and alternate routes. No bridge pre-inspection list, route plan or port coordination protocol sighted.'),
('77919aae-5b25-5fb0-ac6a-8029364d3920'::uuid, '31ccda55-5294-5294-bdf3-daa5fc4f1e84'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CLUP/ZO maps Critical Habitat and Key Biodiversity Area overlay zones and protected areas; CDRA impact chains cover forest and coastal (mangrove) ecosystems; watershed characterization (Malbasag, Pagsanga-an, Haubon) and mangrove restoration are 10-Yr Plan PPAs.'),
('fddc7233-70b2-5eac-9804-b273e515d471'::uuid, '31ccda55-5294-5294-bdf3-daa5fc4f1e84'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) LCCAP 2019-2030 sets coastal (mangrove forest beach, 50 ha in San Antonio, Macabug, Naungan) and forest ecosystem decision areas and a biodiversity assessment; EO 2023-0026 Project TRANSFORM covers biodiversity profiling and nature-based solutions.'),
('d25d825e-e832-5dae-9de7-143df3cbf730'::uuid, 'e26a6095-f517-5af8-9763-0d7818532863'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'watershed PPAs list ENRO, DENR and EDC as partners.'),
('fe383774-bda9-51bf-b87e-0180b868e83a'::uuid, 'b7abd85d-a44b-5e48-8305-6e4e2cb57d52'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'construction-firm MOA for debris clearing and a Drainage and Sewerage Master Plan are planned PPAs (10-Yr Plan); ZO sets river easements.'),
('00f92dee-3e89-5e0d-8992-c16d8a356110'::uuid, 'b7abd85d-a44b-5e48-8305-6e4e2cb57d52'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 08 s.2025 reallocates PHP 2.0 M of the 2025 Trust Fund to drainage works on Malacadios St., Brgy South (flood mitigation); LCCAP lists slope protection on Milagro-Danao roads (CDRRMO, Engineering, barangays) and Pagsangaan River bank stabilisation; CDP PPA 2.12 plans the Drainage and Sewerage Master Plan. These are mitigation works, not pre-impact anticipatory actions.'),
('7367143a-bf22-5381-b2e5-3146434869fe'::uuid, 'b7abd85d-a44b-5e48-8305-6e4e2cb57d52'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(issuances 2021-2024, read 6 Nov 2026) the flood-control and drainage master plan and feasibility study was funded in 2023 (CDRRMC Res. 03, 04 and 07 s.2023, about PHP 11.0 M in total); no output was sighted. Still mitigation, not pre-impact anticipatory action.'),
('8148fff6-9b3c-51fc-bbc2-d56a6670b15b'::uuid, 'e9779a68-4888-59ba-9576-f3bbd3e1344e'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'HEMS/ESU ordinance and DRRM-H plan planned (10-Yr Plan).'),
('a35ecb92-3b5b-5958-8936-bb9e1305aed7'::uuid, 'e9779a68-4888-59ba-9576-f3bbd3e1344e'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDP 2024-2030 PPA 2.15 plans HEMS and Epidemiological Surveillance Unit institutionalisation and a contingency plan for emerging infectious disease; DOH-CHD HEMS and the CHO sit on the CDRRMC; HEMS supervises CPR-RIMT volunteers (SP Res. 2023-347).'),
('66a0904c-651d-588a-b625-3a876b2db5d2'::uuid, '8f86dd62-3f71-5976-bb5a-63abb9717e11'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'school DRRM coordinator training is a 10-Yr Plan PPA; DepEd SDO school AA plans and learning-continuity modalities not sighted.'),
('2b37c775-2bf9-579f-a391-335b3a3e10d3'::uuid, '8f86dd62-3f71-5976-bb5a-63abb9717e11'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) DepEd SDO sits on the CDRRMC (EO 2024-032A) and moved CDRRMC Res. 04 s.2025 (tertiary-institution MOA); CDP PPA 2.16 trains school DRRM coordinators. No school AA plans sighted.'),
('a0971e07-effa-53fb-86a0-dde304571b84'::uuid, '9a85561d-7e4b-53a9-bab4-a8799238c305'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '5,470 farmers (RSBSA 2021) and 5,295 fisherfolk (FishR) registered (10-Yr Plan); buffer seed stock and storage facilities are PPAs; CDRA rates production-area risk by barangay. No early action guidelines sighted.'),
('b4be1f40-7e32-5b2a-9d70-0127ee1989bc'::uuid, '9a85561d-7e4b-53a9-bab4-a8799238c305'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) EO 2023-0042 (19 May 2023) creates the El Nino Task Force chaired by the Mayor, with the City Agriculturist, CSWD, CDRRMO, CPDO, CHO, Engineering, two irrigators'' cooperatives and others, to formulate an El Nino preparedness and rehabilitation plan, monitor it and run an information campaign; LCCAP 2019-2030 plans crop insurance enrolment, climate-ready crop varieties and buffer-stock facilities; CDP PPAs 2.17 (climate-smart agriculture) and 2.21 (El Nino programme).'),
('7f0be9cf-c52e-56ea-910e-6fda8ddb0e80'::uuid, '596b340a-9fb2-582c-925f-cb3ee700d6e9'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'no pre-impact price monitoring arrangement with DTI found; price freeze is treated only as a post-declaration measure under the State of Calamity protocol (A1.6).'),
